# Food Waste Prediction

A Machine Learning project for predicting daily food waste in kilograms using operational food service data.

The project focuses on working with a deliberately messy dataset and applying a complete data preprocessing and machine learning workflow.

---

## Dataset

Source: Kaggle — Messy Food Waste Prediction Dataset

Dataset size: ~900 records across the training and test sets.

The dataset represents operational data from a food service environment. The objective is to predict the amount of food wasted per day based on factors such as meals served, staff experience, waste category, and date information.

---

## Objective

Predict:

`food_waste_kg`

The target represents the amount of food waste generated in kilograms per day.

---

## Features

| Feature | Description | Type |
|---|---|---|
| `date` | Date of the record | Date |
| `meals_served` | Number of meals served during the day | Numerical |
| `staff_experience` | Experience level of the staff | Categorical |
| `waste_category` | Category of food waste | Categorical |
| `food_waste_kg` | Amount of food wasted in kg | Target |

---

## Data Challenges

This dataset was designed to simulate real-world messy data.

The main challenges include:

- Missing values in categorical features
- Outliers in numerical features
- Mixed data types
- Inconsistent categorical values
- Date values requiring preprocessing
- Features requiring transformation before modeling

---

## Data Preprocessing

The preprocessing pipeline includes:

### Missing Values

Missing categorical values are handled using appropriate imputation techniques.

### Categorical Data

Categorical values are cleaned and transformed into numerical representations suitable for machine learning models.

### Date Processing

The `date` column is parsed and decomposed into useful features such as:

- Year
- Month
- Day

### Outlier Handling

Numerical features are inspected for unusual values and potential outliers.

---

## Machine Learning Workflow

The project follows a complete machine learning workflow:

```text
Raw Dataset
     ↓
Data Inspection
     ↓
Data Cleaning
     ↓
Exploratory Data Analysis
     ↓
Feature Engineering
     ↓
Feature Selection
     ↓
Model Training
     ↓
Model Evaluation
     ↓
Prediction
